review('margin-01-focused-ultrasound-drug-delivery-research',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A research concept for focused-ultrasound-assisted drug delivery in adult recurrent glioblastoma, using an existing research platform and a traceable margin-planning workflow.","version":"MARGIN-01 v0.1 research brief, October 21, 2026. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"No prototype, simulation result, clinical performance or novelty is claimed. Published blood–brain-barrier opening and drug-delivery studies motivate investigation but do not validate this proposed combination. More drug delivery or MRI enhancement does not itself establish tumor control or survival benefit. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Mr. Peloquin’s research collection. Codex checked and consolidated objections. The record documents AI-assisted critical review. Individual reviewer contributions remain undocumented. Clinical validation remains open.","sources":"Archived MARGIN-01_Research_Design_Brief.pdf.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2103280118\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-45818-7\nhttps://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-020-65617-6","next":"Establish a useful drug exposure-response window and qualify the existing platform with appropriate specialists before hardware expansion. Separate delivery, biological efficacy and clinical-value gates.","notes":"Engineering research overview only. No treatment settings, eligibility decision or patient-use protocol is provided."});
review('bridge-01-emergency-ecmo-transfer-support-cradle',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A proposed continuously supported transfer cradle for existing portable VA-ECMO equipment, intended to reduce tubing traction during movement between compatible carriers.","version":"BRIDGE-01 v0.3 requirements candidate, October 21, 2026. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"No hardware, bench, blood or human study is demonstrated. Mechanical handoff is the proposed new work; ECMO and commercial transport mounts already exist. Mechanism, interoperability, justified limits and complete resource accounting remain unresolved. It is not ready for scored qualification or human use. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Ray Peloquin with U.I. Grok and Claude reviewed the transport concept; Meta contributed to a nonclinical fixture review. Gemini withdrew unsupported numerical assumptions. None received experimental data.","sources":"Archived BRIDGE-01-requirements-v0.3.md.\nhttps://www.getinge.com/int/products/cardiohelp-system/","next":"Recover the selected equipment's interfaces, establish exploratory mechanical fixtures and independent traction/flow/pressure measurements, then freeze a comparison against a properly configured commercial baseline.","notes":"The cradle does not control therapy or replace specialist clinical care. No new blood-contacting connector or patient-worn loading benefit is established."});
review('cmh-01-contractile-heart-material-research',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A contractile heart-material research candidate: a pressure-driven reinforced compliant architecture intended to convert externally supplied energy into useful chamber work while maintaining a separate blood barrier.","version":"CMH-01 revision 0.1, October 20, 2026. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"No CMH-01 specimen has been manufactured, mechanically tested, blood-tested, aged or implanted. The brief supplies component precedents and checked arithmetic, not a new physical result. Exact material/process selection and the complete system remain open. Architecture-dependent improvement and implant suitability are unestablished. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Ray Peloquin + U.I. One integrating agent and three separate AI reviewers covered the design; this is not a named external-model consultation, laboratory verification or regulatory approval.","sources":"Archived CMH-01_Contractile_Heart_Material_Court_Brief.pdf.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1109/70.481753\nhttps://doi.org/10.1089/soro.2019.0154","next":"Freeze a representative nonclinical module and comparator, then measure loaded work and barrier integrity together before durability and biological qualification claims.","notes":"Public purpose-level summary. Material formulations, geometry, manufacturing details and duty parameters remain outside this record. The material is not a source of energy."});
review('artificial-heart-wireless-power-and-dual-reserves',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A system-level artificial-heart research proposal investigating wireless power and isolated energy reserves alongside established pumping principles.","version":"Artificial heart concept v0.1, October 20, 2026. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"The archive reports an executed two-bank energy model with ten scenarios checked against closed forms and conservation. This is numerical consistency, not device validation. Simulated bank loss is already isolated/open circuit; it does not demonstrate short isolation, thermal containment, voltage stability, circulation or physiological outcomes. No device has been built or tested. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Prepared for Ray Peloquin. Existing pumping, wireless-power and dual-battery approaches are explicitly credited as prior art; no new pumping principle or product superiority is claimed.","sources":"Archived artificial-heart-concept-v0.1.md.\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27401215/\nhttps://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30945635/","next":"Reproduce the energy model, then separately test physical power transfer, failure isolation, mock-loop circulation, thermal behavior and aged energy reserves with qualified device researchers.","notes":"No lifelong reliability, clinical superiority or benefit over a healthy heart is established. Private sizing and component details are omitted. This is not implant-control software."});
review('heartseed-cardiac-support-research',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A hemocompatibility-first artificial-heart architecture concept emphasizing blood interaction, thermal constraints and separation of predictive advice from deterministic protections.","version":"HEARTSEED v1.2 archived state block; standalone current build package not verified. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"The reviewed artifact describes goals and a validation sequence, not measured hemolysis, platelet activation, durability, reserve endurance or implant performance. Proposed geometry optimization and fully implantable operation remain hypotheses. Internal research-direction labels do not certify safety. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Archived Court design from Mr. Peloquin’s research collection. The archived collaboration credits do not assign individual design, implementation, or test contributions.","sources":"Archived Heart of Osiris.txt, HEARTSEED v1.2 state block.","next":"Recover the current source/version history and establish matched computational and nonclinical blood-loop comparators before assigning flow, durability or reserve capability.","notes":"This record is distinct from CMH-01 and the separate wireless/dual-reserve heart proposal. Shared aims do not make their versions or evidence interchangeable. No therapeutic or surgical instructions are supplied."});
review('gips-intramedullary-guidance-and-risk-control',{"expanded":true,"purpose":"A proposed surgeon-controlled intramedullary guidance and risk-control platform, combining corridor visualization, uncertainty, neuromonitoring context and refusal of inadequately supported actions.\n\nRecovered artwork: Earlier illustrated guidance and governance concept; the v0.2 artwork is separate from the previously reviewed v0.5 state block.","version":"GIPS v0.5 state block, May 8, 2026. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.\n\nAdditional visual source: GIPS v0.2.","evidence":"The reviewed document states proposed update rules, intervention tiers and logging requirements, but supplies no hardware, bench or clinical validation report. Its adult-validation wording is unsupported by evidence in that artifact and is not adopted here. Numerical intervention thresholds and performance assertions are unvalidated design inputs. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.\n\nArtwork review: No clinical validation, surgical suitability, pediatric safety, or validated intervention thresholds follow from the illustration. Its numerical and procedural details remain outside the public repository.","contributors":"Archived in Mr. Peloquin's research collection. Individual authorship, implementation and independent validation are not established in the reviewed copy.\n\nRecovered from Mr. Peloquin's collaborative design collection; individual illustration authorship is unverified.","sources":"Archived Pasted text(142).txt, GIPS v0.5 — The Safe Corridor.\nhttps://raypeloquin.github.io/mimirs-well/public-notes/gips-intramedullary-guidance-and-risk-control.md","next":"Recover implementation and source provenance, reconcile unsupported validation language, and define nonclinical registration, sensing-loss, refusal and physical-motion tests before any clinical claim.\n\nArtwork review: Independent clinical and device-safety review; no procedure or human-use instructions are supplied.","notes":"No autonomous spinal-cord exploration or established safe-entry capability. This overview omits intervention settings and does not authorize adult or pediatric clinical use.\n\nOriginal artwork retained outside the public Git repository; purpose-level summary only."});
review('vascular-whisperer-vascular-analysis-and-guidance',{expanded:true,"purpose":"A proposed clinician-facing vascular-imaging research workflow that flags absence, asymmetry and tissue consequences for review, with particular interest in missed distal/medium-vessel occlusions.","version":"Vascular Whisperer v0.3 archived state block. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.","evidence":"The source describes a detection/adjudication architecture and proposed retrospective-to-prospective evaluation path. It contains no trained-model artifact, dataset results, diagnostic accuracy or demonstrated false-negative recovery. Adjudication targets and workflow benefits are not observed outcomes. This website update reviewed the saved source; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.","contributors":"Archived in Mr. Peloquin's research collection; per-stage implementation and individual review attribution remain unresolved.","sources":"Archived VASCULAR WHISPERER v0.3.txt.","next":"Develop an appropriately governed retrospective dataset and independent blinded reference process. Keep training/mining separate from held-out evaluation, report uncertainty and false alerts, and test workflow usefulness before prospective claims.","notes":"No diagnosis or patient triage is performed by this record. Reusing reviewed misses for training must not contaminate the held-out test set."});
