review('mount-olympus-cross-domain-design-and-adversarial-review',{"expanded":true,"purpose":"A proposed design/review methodology for turning ideas into mechanisms, testable claims, explicit evidence levels and accountable decisions.\n\nRecovered artwork: A visual companion to the physics addendum, distinguishing metaphor, interpretation, model, equation and measurement, with a falsifiability gate.","version":"Reviewed physics addendum v1.3P, May 14, 2026, refers back to core v1.2R; later inventory titles do not establish a current consolidated release. Source reviewed November 17, 2026.\n\nAdditional visual source: ARISTOTLE'S LYCEUM ? Mount Olympus v1.3P.","evidence":"The addendum describes separating measurements, equations, models, interpretations and metaphors, and declaring observations that would challenge a claim. It is a review method, not a new physical theory or evidence of better engineering outcomes. Internal approval labels do not establish independent validation. This website update reviewed saved documentation; it did not rerun models or conduct experiments.\n\nArtwork review: The artwork expresses a research method. Decorative equations do not establish a derivation, novel theory or independently replicated result.","contributors":"Court methodology associated with Mr. Peloquin and Asteris; specific contributions belong with each project's provenance.\n\nRecovered from Mr. Peloquin's collaborative design collection; individual illustration authorship is unverified.","sources":"Archived Pasted text(191).txt, Mount Olympus v1.3P physics-review addendum.\nhttps://raypeloquin.github.io/mimirs-well/mount-olympus-cross-domain-design-and-adversarial-review-art.html\nhttps://raypeloquin.github.io/mimirs-well/public-notes/mount-olympus-cross-domain-design-and-adversarial-review.md","next":"Reconcile the core/addendum/version history. Test whether independent readers can recover claim scope, assumptions and decisive failure conditions from a small set of completed review packets.\n\nArtwork review: Apply the documented falsifiability method to specific candidate claims and record disconfirming observations.","notes":"A proposed falsification test must itself be appropriate to the claim and measurement model. Methodological discipline does not make every reviewed conclusion true.\n\nArtwork is preserved as a visual concept, not an operating specification.","publicPage":"mount-olympus-cross-domain-design-and-adversarial-review-art.html"});
